  M4 CANDIDATE [D-talk-request olivia_bennett turns=11 naturalEnd=true]:
    NPC: Olivia: "I've been thinking. You and me — we should be bonded. Not just neighbors. Will you stick with me?"
    YOU: "Yes. Stick together."
    NPC: "Stick together, then." They look steadier already.
    YOU: "How can I help?"
    NPC: "Pantry's thin and getting thinner. Forage with me tomorrow? I know the meadow edge, west of the creek."
    YOU: "I'm listening."
    NPC: "Come get air with me. I need to think out loud."
    YOU: "All right. Let's go."
    NPC: At the ridge the ground is torn up. Something was here, recently, and it wasn't careful. Olivia's hand finds your sleeve. You leave together, faster than you came.
    YOU: "Tell me more."
    NPC: "The pantry's nearly bare. Forage with me tomorrow? I know the ridge above the creek."
    YOU: "Tell me why you need this."
    NPC: "Another day like today and we're choosing who eats. Nobody's worked the ridge above the creek in days. We'll fill packs before dark."
    YOU: Why can’t I do this now?
    NPC: Get to your partner's side of the Haven door and stand next to them — then you can help.
    YOU: Why can’t I do this now?
    NPC: Stand beside your partner first — same side of the Haven door — then help.
    YOU: Why can’t I do this now?
    NPC: Move next to your partner, on the same side of the Haven door.
    YOU: "Yeah?"
    NPC: "Okay. We'll pick this up later."
    YOU: "..."
    NPC: A comfortable quiet settles. They smile a little, and let it be.
