  M4 CANDIDATE [C-friendship quinn_murphy turns=11 naturalEnd=true]:
    NPC: Every wound I close is a small argument against despair.
    NPC: Quinn seems lighter — something good landed recently.
    YOU: "I’m listening."
    NPC: "Every person I patch up is a vote for the world continuing."
    YOU: "Go on."
    NPC: "I learned to set a bone before I learned to read. Hands first, always."
    YOU: "Tell me more."
    NPC: "You look tired. Everyone looks tired. Sit down a minute — no, I'm serious."
    YOU: "I’m listening."
    NPC: "Bodies mend. It's the other stuff — trust, hope — that takes the real work."
    YOU: "Go on."
    NPC: "Every person I help is a vote for the world making sense again."
    YOU: "Tell me more."
    NPC: "I can't save everyone. I can save the person in front of me. Start there."
    YOU: "I’m listening."
    NPC: "I'm not a miracle worker. I'm a witness who brings bandages."
    YOU: "Go on."
    NPC: "Hurt people hurt people. Somebody has to break the chain. Might as well be me."
    YOU: "I’m listening."
    NPC: "Healing's slow. People want it fast. I'm learning to be patient with both."
    YOU: "Go on."
    NPC: "The body wants to heal. Sometimes it just needs someone to believe that with it."
    NPC: "Alright, love. Go do what you need to do."
    YOU: "..."
    NPC: A comfortable quiet settles. They smile a little, and let it be.
    NPC: "This was good." They mean it.

