    NPC: "Can we talk?" Valeria sits down near you. "Just... talk. Like people used to."
    YOU: "I’m listening."
    NPC: "What got you through the first week? The very first days."
    YOU: "Honestly? Shock. Just kept moving."
    NPC: "Look — Shock's underrated. It's the body's way of buying you time."
    YOU: "Take your time."
    NPC: Something in them stays shut, for now.
    YOU: "Take your time."
    NPC: "Spite, mostly. Pure, clean spite at the sky. Then someone shared food with me and the spite turned into something else. I still don't have a word for the something else. Not that it matters."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "Still on what got you through the first week. Simple as that."
    YOU: "Take your time."
    NPC: "You look handy. What did you do with your hands, before?"
    YOU: (tell them your trade)
    NPC: "Useful. Everything useful matters now. I mean that as a compliment."
    YOU: "Take your time."
    NPC: "These hands? Pottery instructor hands. Clipboards, mostly. Now they hold wire and wood, and they learn fast. Hands are honest that way."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "Like I said — we're still on what got you through the first week."
    YOU: "Take your time."
    NPC: "I've got things to see to. Don't be a stranger."
    YOU: "..."
    NPC: "You're a good listener, you know that?" A tired smile.
    NPC: "Good talk. I feel like I know you a little better now."
    NPC: "Take care out there."

