  M4 CANDIDATE [D-talk-request visjoin_99 turns=0 naturalEnd=true]:
    NPC: "About what happened to my taken kin — You talk to it -- the System. Have you ever asked? About the taken -- about Marcelo?"
    YOU: "Yes."
    NPC: "All right. Thank you for telling me."
    YOU: "Yeah?"
    NPC: Something in them stays shut, for now.
    YOU: "Yeah?"
    NPC: "Can I trust you? I mean really."
    YOU: "I hope to earn it."
    NPC: "Hah. That's the right answer. The wrong one would've been 'yes' too fast."
    YOU: "Yeah?"
    NPC: "I'll tell you what I tell everyone: watch what I do when nobody's watching. That's the whole of me. The rest is just talking."
    YOU: "What do you remember?"
    NPC: "It's my brother, Marcelo. Went up in the Taking with the boring half. He was the funniest person I knew. Their metrics are broken. The pods get into my sleep some nights.
    NPC: Row on row of them, humming like a held note -- and I wake up reaching for something that isn't there."
    YOU: "I'll ask it. I promise."
    NPC: "You'd do that? Ask it? ...Thank you. Really. Even asking is more than the silence."
    YOU: "Yeah?"
    NPC: "Still nothing on Marcelo. I told you about the pods -- I keep thinking about them. The humming. Some nights I'm sure it's a dream. Other nights I'm sure it's not."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "Still on that taken person."
    YOU: "Yeah?"
    NPC: Something eases in their shoulders. They're really talking to you now.
    YOU: "Yeah?"
    NPC: "Right. Action time. You know where to find me."
